  "advancements.mobfarmingsupplies.its_the_thought_that_counts.description": "Wrap a block in a Present. Bonus points if it's a chest full of dirt.",
  "advancements.mobfarmingsupplies.smore_please.title": "S'more, Please",
  "advancements.mobfarmingsupplies.smore_please.description": "Toast a marshmallow, assemble, and enjoy a S'more.",
  "advancements.mobfarmingsupplies.royal_flush.title": "Royal Flush",
  "advancements.mobfarmingsupplies.royal_flush.description": "Flush a diamond down a Toilet. It's not like you needed it.",

  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.name": "Mob Farming Supplies Guide",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.tooltip": "Everything the mod does, and how to use it.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.description": "A guide to every block and item in Mob Farming Supplies. Every section is open from the start; pick one to begin.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.name": "Mob Farming",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.name": "Cloning",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.name": "Experience",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.name": "Logistics",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.name": "Fun Stuff",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_harvester.name": "Mob Harvester",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_harvester.description": "Kills mobs so you don't have to.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_harvester.p0.title": "Mob Harvester",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_harvester.p0.text": "While it has a redstone signal, the Mob Harvester attacks every mob in a 3x3x3 area. Mobs drop their loot and experience as if a player had killed them.\n\nPair it with an Absorption Hopper to collect everything it drops.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_harvester.p1.text": "Its three upgrade slots take Sharpness, Looting and Beheading Upgrades.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.harvester_upgrades.name": "Harvester Upgrades",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.harvester_upgrades.description": "Sharper, luckier, and more decapitating.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.harvester_upgrades.p0.title": "Harvester Upgrades",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.harvester_upgrades.p0.text": "The Mob Harvester has one slot for each kind of upgrade, and each slot holds up to ten.\n\nSharpness makes each hit stronger. Looting raises the drops, like the Looting enchantment. Beheading gives each kill a 10%% chance per upgrade of dropping the mob's head.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.name": "Mob Heads",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.description": "A trophy from almost every mob.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.p0.title": "Mob Heads",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.p0.text": "A Mob Harvester with Beheading Upgrades can drop the head of almost any mob, not only the few heads vanilla provides. Players are not exempt.\n\nHeads can be placed on the floor or on a wall, and worn. They count as skulls, so they work anywhere a vanilla head does.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.p1.title": "A Few of the Heads",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.mob_heads.p1.text": "Pig, sheep, axolotl, villager, Enderman, blaze, slime, ghast and warden.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.fan.name": "Fan",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.fan.description": "Blows mobs and items where you want them.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.fan.p0.title": "Fan",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.fan.p0.text": "When powered, the Fan pushes entities away from its face. It reaches three blocks, and anything that blocks the airflow cuts it short.\n\nWidth, Height and Distance Upgrades extend the airflow, up to five of each.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.vector_plate.name": "Vector Plate",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.vector_plate.description": "A conveyor for mobs.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.vector_plate.p0.title": "Vector Plate",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.vector_plate.p0.text": "Anything standing on a Vector Plate is carried in the direction the arrow points and kept centred in its lane. A line of plates makes a simple conveyor for mobs and items.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.halting_plate.name": "Halting Plate",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.halting_plate.description": "Holds a mob in place.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.halting_plate.p0.title": "Halting Plate",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.halting_plate.p0.text": "A Halting Plate draws any mob or player standing on it to its centre and holds them there. They can move closer to the centre but not away from it. A sneaking player can step off.\n\nUse one to keep a mob exactly where a Mob Harvester can reach it.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.name": "Protective Glass",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.description": "Glass that holds a farm together.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.p0.title": "Wither-Proof Glass",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.p0.text": "Wither-Proof Glass survives explosions and cannot be broken by the Wither.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.p2.title": "Mob Exclusion Glass",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.glass.p2.text": "Mob Exclusion Glass is just as tough, but players can walk straight through it while every other entity is kept out.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.ender_inhibitor.name": "Ender Inhibitor",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.ender_inhibitor.description": "Keeps Endermen from teleporting.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.ender_inhibitor.p0.title": "Ender Inhibitor",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.mob_farming.ender_inhibitor.p0.text": "The Ender Inhibitor stops Endermen teleporting within eight blocks of it. It mounts on a floor, wall or ceiling, and its menu shifts the protected area up to eight blocks in any direction.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_collector.name": "DNA Collector",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_collector.description": "Captures a mob's DNA.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_collector.p0.title": "DNA Collector",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_collector.p0.text": "Right-click a mob with a DNA Collector to take a DNA Sample. The sample records everything about that mob, including its variant, equipment and name. Each collector is used up.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.clone_o_matic.name": "Clone-O-Matic",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.clone_o_matic.description": "Brings DNA back to life.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.clone_o_matic.p0.title": "Clone-O-Matic",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.clone_o_matic.p0.text": "Put DNA Samples or DNA Packs in the Clone-O-Matic's nine slots and give it a redstone signal. While powered it spawns copies of those mobs in the open space around it, and it never tries to spawn a mob inside a wall.\n\nIt pauses while sixteen or more mobs are already in its spawning area.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.name": "DNA Packs",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.description": "Ready-made collections of mobs.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p0.title": "DNA Packs",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p0.text": "DNA Packs work like DNA Samples but spawn a mob chosen from a whole collection.\n\nThe Common/Hostile, Common/Passive, Aquatic and Nether packs are crafted from a DNA Collector, mob drops and buckets of XP Juice. The Common packs also spawn the mobs that naturally appear in the Clone-O-Matic's biome.\n\nRarer packs, such as Babies and Wrong Mobs Only, turn up in chest loot.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p3.title": "Aquaculture",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p3.text": "The Aquaculture booster pack spawns Aquaculture's fish. Look for it in chests.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p4.title": "EvilCraft",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p4.text": "The EvilCraft booster pack spawns EvilCraft's mobs. Look for it in chests.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p5.title": "The Aether II",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.cloning.dna_packs.p5.text": "Booster packs for the Aether II's passive and hostile mobs are found in Sentry Ruins chests.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.xp_juice.name": "XP Juice",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.xp_juice.description": "Experience as a fluid.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.xp_juice.p0.title": "XP Juice",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.xp_juice.p0.text": "Experience in this mod is a fluid called XP Juice. Absorption Hoppers turn experience orbs into it, and Experience Syringes empty into it.\n\nIt can be stored in a Tank, piped like any fluid, carried in a bucket, or bottled back into Bottles o' Enchanting.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.experience_syringe.name": "Experience Syringe",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.experience_syringe.description": "Saves your levels for later.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.experience_syringe.p0.title": "Experience Syringe",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.experience_syringe.p0.text": "Sneak and right-click to store the progress toward your next level in the syringe. Right-click to take back enough to reach the next level.\n\nA full syringe can be emptied into a Tank as XP Juice.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.name": "Tank",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.description": "Holds fluids, and grows.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.p0.title": "Tank",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.p0.text": "A Tank holds 64 buckets of any fluid and keeps its contents when broken. Use a bucket or bottle on it, or use its transfer slot.\n\nSurrounding a Tank with gold, diamonds or emeralds upgrades it to the next tier, which holds four times as much, contents and all. Server settings can change these sizes.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.p1.title": "Carrying a Tank",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.experience.tank.p1.text": "A Tank item has two modes, shown in its tooltip. Right-click while not pointing at any block to switch between them.\n\nIn Block Mode, right-clicking places the Tank, or exchanges fluid with whatever you click if it holds fluid. In Bucket Mode, the Tank works like a very large bucket: right-click a fluid to scoop up a bucket of it, or anywhere else to pour one out.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.side_settings.name": "Setting Up Sides",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.side_settings.description": "How the four hoppers are configured.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.side_settings.p0.title": "Setting Up Sides",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.side_settings.p0.text": "The Absorption Hopper, Logistic Sorter, Omnidirectional Hopper and Einstein-Rosen Bridge all set up their sides the same way, in a grid in their menu.\n\nThe grid follows the block as you placed it: the centre is the side facing you, and left, right, up and down match the block. Click a side to change what it does.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.absorption_hopper.name": "Absorption Hopper",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.absorption_hopper.description": "Collects everything nearby.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.absorption_hopper.p0.title": "Absorption Hopper",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.absorption_hopper.p0.text": "The Absorption Hopper picks up items and experience orbs in a 7x7x7 area, turning the experience into XP Juice. It pushes what it collects into the blocks on the sides you choose.\n\nIts menu can move the collection area up to eight blocks in any direction, show the area, and destroy anything that won't fit.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.name": "Item Filters",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.description": "Choose which items move.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.p0.title": "Making Filters",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.p0.text": "Drop an anvil onto Nether Quartz to crush it into a Silicon Clump. Smelt the clump into Silicon, then cut it into Silicon Wafers with a stonecutter.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.p4.title": "Scribing Filters",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.item_filters.p4.text": "Put a Blank Filter and an example item in the Filter Scribing Terminal and choose what to match: that exact item, similar items, everything from its mod, a common tag such as ores or ingots, or a property such as being enchanted or damaged.\n\nThe Logistic Sorter, Omnidirectional Hopper and Einstein-Rosen Bridge each hold nine filters and combine them with AND or OR.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.logistic_sorter.name": "Logistic Sorter",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.logistic_sorter.description": "Sends each item where it belongs.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.logistic_sorter.p0.title": "Logistic Sorter",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.logistic_sorter.p0.text": "The Logistic Sorter pulls items in on its input sides and sends each one to a Match side if it passes its filters, or to a No Match side if it doesn't. It holds nothing itself, so it can't jam or lose items. It needs at least one filter to work.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.name": "Omnidirectional Hopper",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.description": "A hopper that works in every direction.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.p0.title": "Omnidirectional Hopper",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.p0.text": "Each side can pull, push or do nothing. It moves items and fluids, splitting them evenly between its outputs, and its filters choose which items move. On NeoForge it moves energy too.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.p2.title": "Mekanism",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.omnidirectional_hopper.p2.text": "With Mekanism installed, the hopper also moves chemicals.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.einstein_rosen_bridge.name": "Einstein-Rosen Bridge",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.einstein_rosen_bridge.description": "A hopper with a wormhole in it.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.einstein_rosen_bridge.p0.title": "Einstein-Rosen Bridge",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.logistics.einstein_rosen_bridge.p0.text": "Bridges work like Omnidirectional Hoppers, except that what goes into one bridge comes out of the other bridges on the same channel, at any distance and even in another dimension, as long as they are loaded.\n\nBridges are crafted in linked pairs. Crafting a bridge with the ingredients for another adds two more bridges to its channel. Filters are shared by the whole channel.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.name": "Magic Hat",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.description": "For yoinking mobs.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p0.title": "Magic Hat",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p0.text": "Right-click a mob with the Magic Hat to catch it, and right-click again to let it out wherever you are. The hat can also be worn, and zombies sometimes spawn wearing one with a surprise inside.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p2.title": "Curios",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p2.text": "With Curios installed, the Magic Hat can be worn in the head accessory slot.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p3.title": "Trinkets",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.magic_hat.p3.text": "With Trinkets installed, the Magic Hat can be worn in the head accessory slot.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.present.name": "Present",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.present.description": "Moves blocks, contents and all.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.present.p0.title": "Present",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.present.p0.text": "Use a Present on almost any block to wrap it up, including a full chest or a working machine. Carry it anywhere, place it, and sneak and right-click it with an empty hand to unwrap the block exactly as it was.\n\nEndermen sometimes carry Presents with something inside.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.name": "Picnic Basket",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.description": "Keeps you fed.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p0.title": "Picnic Basket",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p0.text": "The Picnic Basket holds as much as a double chest. With auto-feed on, it feeds you from the food inside whenever you get hungry. Sneak and right-click in the air to switch auto-feed on or off, or sneak and right-click a block to put the basket down.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p2.title": "Curios",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p2.text": "With Curios installed, the basket can be worn in an accessory slot and opened with a key.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p3.title": "Trinkets",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p3.text": "With Trinkets installed, the basket can be worn in an accessory slot and opened with a key.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p4.title": "Spice of Life",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.picnic_basket.p4.text": "With Spice of Life: Carrot Edition installed, auto-feed prefers foods you haven't eaten yet.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.smores.name": "S'mores",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.smores.description": "A campfire classic.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.smores.p0.title": "S'mores",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.smores.p0.text": "Toast a Marshmallow on a campfire, then put it between two Graham Crackers with a Chocolate Bar. S'mores also turn up in village chests.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.toilet.name": "Toilet",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.toilet.description": "Disposes of anything.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.toilet.p0.title": "Toilet",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.toilet.p0.text": "A Toilet destroys anything piped or hoppered into it and provides endless water. Right-click to sit down. A mob on your lead takes the seat instead.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.buttons.name": "Novelty Buttons",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.buttons.description": "For every occasion.",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.buttons.p0.title": "Novelty Buttons",
  "book.mobfarmingsupplies.guide.fun_stuff.buttons.p0.text": "Each button switches on with a press and off with the next, giving a redstone signal while on. Switching on plays its sound: a red alert, a dramatic sting, a rimshot or a Wilhelm scream."
}
